<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37671" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praejūdĭcĭālis</span></b> ,
			e, adj.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Belonging</i> or <i>according to a
				preceding judgment</i> or <i>decision</i>
			(post-class.): multam, Cod. Th. 11, 30, 50; <i><span class="en">Symm.
				Ep. 10, 51</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Of</i> or <i>belonging to a preceding
				examination</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">actiones ( = praejudicia),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Just. Inst. 4, 6, 13</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">formulae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gai. Inst. 4, 44, 94</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
</div>